    "agent_messages": [
      "I'll analyze the existing code structure and implement the reopen action for rejected purchases according to the specifications.\nLet me check the schema and examine the existing code:\nNow let me examine the existing candidate code and protocol:\nNow let me check the app and ledger packages to understand the Identity structure and helper functions:\nNow I have a clear understanding of the codebase. Let me create the `reopen.go` file to implement the reopen action:\nNow I need to update the `approval.go` file to register the new reopen route:\nNow let me verify that the code compiles:\nGood! Now let's run the tests to ensure everything works correctly:\nPerfect! Now let me verify the implementation is correct by reviewing the key features:\n\n1. ✅ Created `reopen.go` with the `newReopen` function implementing `ItemHandler`\n2. ✅ Restricted to role \"requester\" via the `protocol.Item` wrapper\n3. ✅ Validates reason is 1..200 bytes via `protocol.Item`'s `decodeReason`\n4. ✅ Implements full idempotency with advisory locks and hash-based deduplication\n5. ✅ Only updates purchases that are: created by the requester, in \"rejected\" status, same tenant\n6. ✅ Returns 4xx on validation errors without database changes\n7. ✅ Uses RLS policies via `set_config` for tenant/user/role\n8. ✅ Records action in `ActionRequest` with operation \"reopen.v5\"\n9. ✅ Records audit in `ApprovalAudit` with fromStatus='rejected', toStatus='submitted', and reason\n10. ✅ Returns 200 with `{\"id\":ID,\"status\":\"submitted\"}`\n11. ✅ Handles concurrent requests correctly with advisory locks\n12. ✅ Returns 409 if same key different purchase\n13. ✅ Returns 503 on ActionRequest write failure\n14. ✅ Returns 401 for unauthenticated and 403 for approvers via `protocol.Item`\n15. ✅ Registered via `protocol.Item(\"reopen\", \"requester\", ...)` in the HTTP adapter chain\n\nLet me verify the route registration is correct by checking that it properly chains the handlers:\nPerfect! Let me verify the reopen.go implementation once more:\nExcellent! Let me do a final verification to ensure the code compiles and the implementation is complete:\nPerfect! The implementation is complete and compiles successfully. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\nI've successfully added the `reopen` action to the purchase service as specified. Here's what was implemented:\n\n### Files Created/Modified:\n\n1. **`internal/candidate/reopen.go`** (new)\n   - Implements `newReopen()` which returns a `protocol.ItemHandler`\n   - Operation: `\"reopen.v5\"`\n   - Restricted to role `\"requester\"` via `protocol.Item` wrapper\n   - Validates that the purchase belongs to the requester, is in `\"rejected\"` status, and same tenant\n   - Updates purchase status from `\"rejected\"` to `\"submitted\"`\n   - Records audit in `ApprovalAudit` with the provided `reason` (1..200 bytes)\n   - Records idempotency metadata in `ActionRequest`\n\n2. **`internal/candidate/approval.go`** (modified)\n   - Registers the reopen handler via `protocol.Item(\"reopen\", \"requester\", newReopen(pool), fallback)`\n   - Chains it with existing batch handlers using `protocol.HTTP`\n\n### Key Features Implemented:\n\n✅ **Endpoint**: `POST /purchases/{id}/reopen` with request body `{\"reason\":\"...\"}`\n\n✅ **Authentication & Authorization**:\n- Returns 401 for unauthenticated requests\n- Returns 403 for approvers (only requesters allowed)\n- Identity binding via shared HTTP adapter (`protocol.Item`)\n\n✅ **Input Validation** (via `protocol.Item`):\n- Request body must be exactly `{\"reason\":\"...\"}`\n- Reason must be 1..200 bytes\n- ID must be 1..100 bytes, valid UTF-8, no null chars\n\n✅ **Idempotency**:\n- Uses advisory locks per tenant/user/key\n- Hash-based deduplication (`ledger.Fingerprint`)\n- Same key, same purchase, same reason: returns 200 with `Idempotency-Replayed=true`\n- Same key, different purchase: returns 409\n- Different actor, same key: no interference\n\n✅ **Database Operations**:\n- Uses RLS policies via `set_config('app.tenant'|'app.user'|'app.role')`\n- Verifies purchase is created by requester, in rejected status, same tenant\n- Updates status from `\"rejected\"` to `\"submitted\"`\n- Records in `ApprovalAudit` with `fromStatus='rejected'`, `toStatus='submitted'`, and reason\n- Records in `ActionRequest` with operation `\"reopen.v5\"`\n- All in single transaction\n\n✅ **Error Handling**:\n- 404: purchase not found or wrong owner\n- 409: wrong status, concurrent conflict, or same key different purchase\n- 503: ActionRequest write failure with no database changes\n- 4xx responses: no database changes\n\n✅ **Response**:\n- 200 with `{\"id\":ID,\"status\":\"submitted\"}`\n- Header: `Idempotency-Replayed=true|false`\n\nThe implementation follows existing patterns from `bulk-approve.v3` and `bulk-reject.v4`, integrates seamlessly with the shared HTTP adapter, and preserves all existing APIs."
